<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Straits Settlements</h1><p class="st-meta">1826 CE – 1946 CE · capital Singapore</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">British colony uniting Penang, Malacca and Singapore, the commercial hub of British Malaya for over a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-dutch-treaty-of-1824">Anglo-Dutch Treaty of 1824</a> secured <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-malacca">Dutch Malacca</a> for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> in 1826 joined it with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-of-wales-island">Prince of Wales Island</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penang">Penang</a>) and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/singapore">Singapore</a> into a single presidency. The seat of government moved from Penang to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> in 1832.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The settlements were ruled from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-raj">British India</a> until 1867, when they became a crown colony under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colonial-office">Colonial Office</a>, administered by a governor with executive and legislative councils. Free trade made <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/singapore">Singapore</a> a great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepot</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a>, opium and textiles. The governor also served as High Commissioner for the protected Malay states, and Chinese and Indian immigrants formed a majority.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> occupied the colony from 1942 to 1945. In 1946 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> dissolved the Straits Settlements: <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/singapore">Singapore</a> became the separate <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-singapore">Colony of Singapore</a>, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-of-wales-island">Penang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/malayan-union">Malayan Union</a>, later becoming states of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/malaysia">Malaysia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/straits-settlements.jpg" alt="Straits Settlements" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Flag_of_the_British_Straits_Settlements_(1874-1942).svg: Himasaram derivative work: Sderftgyvjkoljoyvgtfrd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_British_Straits_Settlements_(1925%E2%80%931946).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1826 CE – 1946 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Singapore</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Andrew Clarke, Frank Swettenham</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Chinese folk religion, Buddhism, Hinduism, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Malay, Chinese, Tamil</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/singapore">Singapore</a>, <a href="/countries/malaysia">Malaysia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Colony of the Straits Settlements</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1886&amp;focus=straits-settlements" aria-label="Straits Settlements on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7563 2129 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Straits Settlements lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7883 2385L7839 2352M7883 2385L7781 2231M7883 2385L4997 651M7883 2385L7364 1601M7883 2385L7364 1602M7883 2385L7823 2316M7883 2385L7883 2385M7883 2385L8195 2236"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7839 2352h0M7781 2231h0M4997 651h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7823 2316h0M7883 2385h0M8195 2236h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7883 2385h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7883 2385h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Singapore. <a href="/atlas?year=1886&amp;focus=straits-settlements">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
